$.bMY=function(){var s=u._,r=t.s,q=A.b5("ae<a8<z>>")
return A.a([A.a([A.a(["Terms of Use",u.N],r),A.a(["1. Definitions and Interpretation",u.O],r),A.a([u.m,u.c],r),A.a(["3. Quality of the Facilitation Services",u.A],r),A.a(["4. The Professional\u2019s obligations",u.a],r),A.a(["5. Purchasing & Using Credits",u.x],r),A.a(["6. Refunding Credits",u.w],r),A.a(["7. Intellectual Property Rights",u.F],r),A.a(["8. Data Protection",u.B],r),A.a(["9. Liability",u.y],r),A.a(["10. Information & Confidentiality",u.Q],r),A.a(["11. Termination",u.Z],r),A.a(["12. General provisions",u.n],r),A.a(["Contact Us",s],r)],q),A.a([A.a(["Privacy Policy","Reno Research Privacy Policy\n\n*Privacy Policy*\n\nThis Policy applies to the collection, use, and disclosure of an individual customer\u2019s Personal Data by Reno Research Pte Ltd and its affiliates (collectively \u201cReno Research\u201d).\n\n1. General\nThis Policy outlines the obligations and practices of Reno Research regarding Personal Data.\nReno Research will use reasonable efforts to respect the confidentiality of Personal Data. By interacting with us, you consent to the collection, use, and disclosure of your Personal Data as described in this Policy.\nThis Policy supplements other consents you may have given regarding your Personal Data.\n\u201cPersonal Data\u201d means data about an individual who can be identified from that data or from that data and other information Reno Research has access to.\n\n2. Statement of Practices\nPersonal Data collected may include: name, address, phone number, email, or any other details necessary to help service your enquiry.\n\nWe use cookies on our websites. You can set your browser to refuse cookies if you prefer.\n\n3. Purpose of Collection\nPersonal Data is collected for matching to service providers, internal training, market research, direct contact, and informing you of new services.\n\nPersonal Data may be disclosed within Reno Research, it may be disclosed to third parties such as regulators, law enforcement, lawyers, auditors, service providers, and potential buyers.\n\nPersonal Data may also be disclosed as required by law, for legal proceedings, to establish or defend legal rights, or with your consent.\n\n4. Optional Data Provision\nAdditional data may be requested to improve services, but it is optional.\n\nCalls to service hotlines may be recorded for quality control and training purposes.\n\n5. Requesting Data Deletion\nYou can request the deletion of your Personal Data.\nEmail your deletion requests to hello@renoresearch.sg. We will delete your data unless retention is legally required. If we cannot delete your data, we will inform you of the reasons.\n\nDeletion of data may affect our ability to provide services.\nRequests will be processed within thirty (30) days.\n\n6. Transfer of Personal Data Overseas\nPersonal Data may be processed in jurisdictions outside Singapore. Reno Research will comply with the Act.\n\n7. Accuracy of Personal Data\nReno Research will use reasonable efforts to ensure data accuracy and will update data upon notification. We uses safeguards to protect Personal Data but cannot guarantee absolute security.\n\n8. Access and Correction of Personal Data\nYou have the right to:\na) Check if Reno Research holds your Personal Data and obtain copies.\nb) Request correction of inaccurate Personal Data.\n\nA reasonable fee may be charged for access requests.\nProof of identity may also be required for data access or correction.\n\n9. Accessing and Deleting Personal Information\nSingapore residents can request disclosure of collected personal information. You may also request the deletion of personal information. Requests should be sent via email to hello@renoresearch.sg.\n\nAdditional information may be required for identity verification.\nRetention of certain information may be necessary for legal, security, or business reasons.\n\n10. Storage and Retention of Personal Data\nPersonal Data will be deleted or anonymized when no longer needed for business or legal purposes.\n\n11. Contacting You\nBy providing contact information, you consent to being contacted for purposes stated in this Policy, even if your contact information is listed on the Do Not Call Registry.\n\n12. Change Policy\nReno Research reserves the right to alter this Policy, should the need arises for business or legal purposes. If you do not agree to the changes, inform us as soon as possible.\n\n13. Governing Law\nThis Policy is governed by the laws of Singapore, and disputes shall be subject to the jurisdiction of Singapore courts.\n\n14. Miscellaneous\nThis Policy does not cover third-party sites linked to Reno Research.\nReno Research will not sell your personal information to third parties without your permission, there will be a form (online or offline) that has agreed to using your information to serve your enquiry.\n\n15. The website is not intended for children under 18, and Reno Research does not knowingly collect information from them.\n16. Contacting the Data Protection Officer\nYou can request access to or correction of your Personal Data within thirty (30) days.\nYou can also send complaints or feedback to the Data Protection Officer (DPO) at hello@renoresearch.sg.\nIf your personal data was provided by a third party, contact them for inquiries.\nTo opt out of the use of your Personal Data for specific purposes, email the DPO. This may affect our ability to serve you.\n\nYou can also contact us at +65 8088 0201\n"],r)],q),A.a([A.a(["Cookie Policy",u.L],r),A.a(["What Are Cookies?",u.i],r),A.a(["How We Use Cookies",u.b],r),A.a(["Types of Cookies We Use",""],r),A.a(["Essential Cookies",u.k],r),A.a(["Performance Cookies",u.g],r),A.a(["Functional Cookies",u.W],r),A.a(["Third-Party Cookies",u.z],r),A.a(["Google Analytics",u.ax],r),A.a(["Your Choices Regarding Cookies",u.j0],r),A.a(["Managing Cookies",u.l],r),A.a(["Changes to This Cookie Policy",u.R],r),A.a(["Contact Us",s],r)],q)],A.b5("ae<a8<a8<z>>>"))}()
